//! GENERATED BY `tests/cli.rs` — the header half of the incremental-ratchet
//! fixture. Never compiled: it is written into a throwaway git repo at whatever
//! path the committed `pdiag-baseline.txt` names in its first row, so the
//! detector sees a file it already has an allowance for.
//!
//! Paired with `site_block.rs.template`, which is appended N times to hit
//! an EXACT code-less count. `tests/cli.rs` writes it twice: once at N = the
//! baseline row (live == baseline, no verdict, exit 0), then at N + 1 (live >
//! baseline, one `Exceeded` High, exit 1). That second write is the ratchet's
//! load-bearing direction — a file ALREADY in the baseline going up by one —
//! which the `NewFile`-on-an-empty-baseline scenarios cannot reach.
//!
//! Deliberately carries no `.with_code(` and no reviewed opt-out token: every
//! site below must stay code-less, or the count the test computes would not be
//! the count the detector sees.
//!
//! `.rs.template`, not `.rs`, so cargo never mistakes the fixture for a test
//! target. It is doubly outside PDIAG's own sweep regardless — a `tests` path
//! segment AND the `crates/reify-audit/` scope exclusion.
